// wolf_hello.lu — px10's gap-census subject: the smallest wolf program
// that prints, built by tools/mkwolf-hello with the pinned wolf
// (`--release`) and linked static against the host's glibc (the census's
// `cc -static` shape, docs/CENSUS.md), then run on PAX from the
// initramfs as /bin/wolf-hello: every system call it makes that PAX
// lacks is a `-ENOSYS` line, so its transcript is the gap to M-PX3.
fn main() {
    print("hello from wolf, linked static, run unmodified\n")
}
